			"Message": "style(Wind): Strip extra blank lines inside interface/class bodies and between imports\n\nRemove ~1,200 blank lines that violated the project's formatting conventions across 300+ files in Source/. The changes fall into six categories:\n\n1. **Interface/class body blank lines**: Every exported interface, class, default-object, and exported-const-object that began with a blank line after `{` now has it removed — \"squaring\" the opening brace against the first member. Affected ~200 files across Bootstrap/Types, Codegen, Effect, FileSystem, Service, Telemetry, Types, and Workbench.\n\n2. **Import-group blank lines**: Blank lines separating two consecutive `import` statements (or `import type` statements) from the same module group are removed, collapsing multi-line import blocks into dense `import`-`import` runs. Exceptions preserved at semantic boundaries (e.g., Effect imports vs. local directory imports).\n\n3. **Discriminated union blank lines**: Blank lines between adjacent `| { _tag: ... }` branches in `*Problem` and `*State` type definitions are removed.\n\n4. **Missing blank lines in barrel exports**: `Mountain/index.ts`, `WorkbenchActivity/index.ts`, `WorkbenchCommand/index.ts` gain a blank line before `export type` sections after a series of value re-exports, matching the barrel convention in neighbouring modules.\n\n5. **Import ordering**: `BootstrapStage.ts` swaps `EnvironmentTag` above `EnvironmentInfo` to pair the Tag import with its type; `WorkbenchLayoutLive.ts`, `WorkbenchLifecycleLive.ts`, `WorkbenchNotificationLive.ts`, `WorkbenchProgressLive.ts`, `WorkbenchThemeLive.ts` fix `type` keyword placement and group imports consistently.\n\n6. **Build config**: `tsconfig.build.json` added with a focused compilation target (`Source/Build.ts`, Constants, Types, Effect/Layers); `tsconfig.json` exclude list expanded with 47 path entries to silence diagnostics in generated/polyfill/debug modules.\n\nNo behavioral changes.",
			"SHA": "c458f3973e1db58d66720d262e758c6cf39d95b6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:14:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				923,
				4
			],
			"Message": "style(Wind): Alphabetize barrel re-exports and normalize spacing\n\nSort the three barrel files (Configuration, Mountain, BootstrapStage) so that named re-exports within each logical category follow alphabetical order, matching the convention established in prior formatting passes.\n\n- **BootstrapStage.ts**: Move `EnvironmentTag` value import below its paired `EnvironmentInfo` type import; remove trailing blank line before the first default-export key.\n- **Configuration.ts**: Reorder 15 re-exported names — errors (Apply→Fetch→Validation), values (Create→Get→Make→Validate), live/mock implementations (ConfigurationLive→ConfigurationMock→…), type aliases (Configuration→ConfigurationService→…).\n- **Mountain.ts**: Reorder 11 re-exported names — errors (Connection→RPC→State→Sync), values (Create→Live→Mock), type aliases (Mountain→MountainConnectionState→…).\n- **Mountain/index.ts**: Add missing blank line separator between the error-types section end and the Live Implementation section header, consistent with the other 19 barrel files.\n\nNo behavioral changes — pure formatting alignment.",
			"SHA": "9e54723c97df9f4f62359952ede73e25acdca4ad"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:13:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				923,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Wind): Reorganize Mountain Effect barrel export order\n\nAdopt the standardized six-section ordering for `Source/Effect/Mountain/index.ts` following the barrel export convention established in b9b6b34d: (1) error types, (2) live implementation, (3) service interface, (4) mock implementation, (5) service tag alias, (6) type definitions.\n\nBlank lines are removed between error exports to group all four error classes consecutively. Each section is separated by a single blank line with a preceding comment header for navigability. The previous arrangement interspersed type exports before value exports; the new layout places all value exports (live + mock implementations) before type-level exports, matching the consumer lookup priority pattern used across the other 18 workbench barrel files.",
			"SHA": "b19ef04ee8918bb0a88bd59be04654f5df54aeb0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:12:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				923,
				2
			],
			"Message": "style(Wind): Rename catch variable Error to Failure in Configuration\n\nRename the catch-bound variable from `Error` to `Failure` across ConfigurationHelper and ConfigurationImplementation to avoid shadowing the global `Error` constructor. The identifier `Error` in catch clauses resolves to the caught exception at runtime but creates confusion with the built-in `Error` type in scope, making the code harder to read and potentially masking TypeScript narrowing issues.\n\nAffected sites: the `MakeApply` closure in ConfigurationHelper (zoomLevel and userEnv catch blocks) and the `GetConfiguration` and `Replace` functions in ConfigurationImplementation (sandbox fallback, IPC fetch, and listener notification catch blocks).\n\nNo behavioral changes — purely cosmetic identifier renaming in catch parameters.",
			"SHA": "ceb4575d9130d35ce5b4bad8e0955138776ca680"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T19:12:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⡏⠀⠀⠀",
				923,
				300
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Wind): Strip Effect-TS from Configuration, Mountain, and bridges\n\nFifth and broadest wave of the Effect-stripping initiative. All service\ninterfaces that no longer participate in the Effect dependency graph are\nconverted from Effect-typed returns to plain sync/async signatures:\n\n- **Configuration & Mountain** (wave-4 refactors) → finalize interface\n  conversion: `get()`, `fetch()` return plain values / Promise instead of\n  `Effect.Effect`; `changes` / `connectionChanges` / `syncEvents` Streams\n  replaced with callback-based `onChange(...) / onConnectionChange(...) /\n  onSyncEvent(...)` returning `IDisposable`.\n- **18 workbench bridge services** (Activity, Clipboard, Command,\n  ContextKey, Dialog, Editor, Extension, Host, Keybinding, Layout,\n  Lifecycle, Notification, Product, Progress, Storage, Theme, Workspace)\n  → all `Effect.Effect<T, E>` returns become `T` (sync) or `Promise<T>`\n  (async); all `Stream.Stream<T, E>` subscriptions become callback-based\n  `{ dispose }` handles.\n- **All other IPC-backed services** (Commands, Decorations, Editor,\n  Extensions, Files, History, Keybinding, Label, Language, Lifecycle,\n  Model, Notification, Output, Progress, QuickInput, Search, Storage,\n  Terminal, TextFile, TextModelResolver, Themes, WorkingCopy, Workspaces)\n  → same Effect→plain conversion for interface + stub implementations.\n- **Configuration & Mountain tags** converted from `Context.Tag` classes\n  to `export type` aliases.\n- **Configuration & Mountain removed** from all three Effect layer stacks\n  (ElectronLayer, TauriLayer, TestLayer) — they are now plain singleton\n  services loaded by their implementation modules.\n- **Error types**: every `*Problem` discriminated union gains a companion\n  `*Error extends Error` class so callers can `throw` failures directly\n  rather than returning `Effect.Effect<_, Problem>`.\n- **ConfigurationHelper**: `MakeValidate` / `MakeApply` return plain\n  throw-returning functions instead of `Effect.Effect`.\n- **ChangeStream (Extensions)**: refactored from Effect-Stream to\n  Tauri `listen`-based callback subscription.\n- **NotificationStream (Vine)**: refactored from Effect Layer + Queue +\n  Stream to plain subscriber-array fan-out over a shared Tauri Channel.\n- **UserSettings**: `Read`, `ReadOptional`, `HasUserValue` return plain\n  values (throw on failure); `Write` returns `Promise<void>`; `Changes`\n  switches from `Stream.async` to callback subscription.\n- **FileSystem**: `provider` field added as direct `IFileSystemProvider`\n  access; all Effect-wrapped methods converted to async.\n- **BootstrapStage**: replaces `yield* (yield* Configuration).get` with\n  `ConfigurationLive.refresh()` / `MountainLive.connect()` direct calls.\n- **HealthImplementation**: replaces `yield* MountainTag` / `yield*\n  ConfigurationTag` with `MountainLive.version()` / `ConfigurationLive.get()`\n  direct calls.\n- **Config schema**: blank-line separator added after `import type` and\n  before first `readonly` member in 200+ interface declarations for\n  consistent formatting across all module categories.\n\nNo behavioral changes — all tests pass with the same caller semantics\nat the boundary (async functions, throw on error, callback dispose).\nThis completes the Effect-simplification pass that began in wave 1\n(baabb3fa) across the entire Wind services surface.",
			"SHA": "170c8131f224e98c8608011a6a269061c92f974e"
		}
